{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1518545521,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NTM1NDIzNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2160#issuecomment-365354237"},"message":"just randomly ran into what might come handy: https://github.com/juhakivekas/multidiff  (FWIW in Python as well)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518639946,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NTczNDI1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2160#issuecomment-365734259"},"message":"From the perspective of `diff` it would be easy to add such a feature. It is practically just an alternative \"result_renderer\", as the results already contain all info. Here is an example of a file that I `git mv`'ed in a subdataset:\n\n```\n{\n  \"action\": \"diff\", \n  \"mode\": 33188, \n  \"mode_src\": 33188, \n  \"parentds\": \"/tmp/aggdemo/openfmri\", \n  \"path\": \"/tmp/aggdemo/openfmri/mike\", \n  \"path_src\": \"/tmp/aggdemo/openfmri/datapackage.json\", \n  \"perc_similarity\": 91.0, \n  \"refds\": \"/tmp/aggdemo\", \n  \"revision\": \"0690366164b8aa515b60fd647c58ffe63e396a3b\", \n  \"revision_src\": \"62dc679772dd12479249985d865977e76dcaf126\", \n  \"state\": \"renamed\", \n  \"status\": \"ok\", \n  \"type\": \"file\", \n  \"type_src\": \"file\"\n}\n```\n\nYou can see that all revision info and path (changes) are represented. However, there is a whole new level of complexity being added by all the combinations of old/new version of annexed files present/absent.\n\nFTR: The API for result renderers is\n\n```\ndef custom_result_renderer(res, **kwargs):\n```\n\nwhere `res` is a result status dict (as shown above), and `kwargs` are all the args that the original command received (so it would get to see a `--content` flag too). The renderer is called once for each item that comes out of the generator, and a content diff renderen could be produced when all conditions are met: has to be a file (before and after), content is locally available, etc.\n\nI am afraid that we will also have to add a few metric tons of formating and filtering options (see `git diff` for the attractor state ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1543050896,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTM1NDIyNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2160#issuecomment-441354226"},"message":"Same as #2812","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1545124715,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0ODE1MTQ1MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2160#issuecomment-448151451"},"message":"Here is a quick update on what information is available to a renderer implementation with the ability to display diffs with the code in https://github.com/datalad/datalad-revolution/pull/58/commits/cd733da9fe742f4424038ab07a27dd9d7372de71 (which is part of https://github.com/datalad/datalad-revolution/pull/58)\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad rev-create differ\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/differ \ncreate(ok): /tmp/differ (dataset)                                                                                            \n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % cd differ\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/differ (git)-[master] % echo 123 \u003e demo.txt\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/differ (git)-[master] % datalad rev-save\nadd(ok): demo.txt (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/differ (git)-[master] % datalad unlock demo.txt\nunlock(ok): /tmp/differ/demo.txt (file)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/differ (git)-[master] % echo 456 \u003e demo.txt\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/differ (git)-[master] % datalad rev-save\nadd(ok): demo.txt (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp/differ (git)-[master] % datalad -f json_pp rev-diff --annex all -f HEAD~1 demo.txt \n{\n  \"action\": \"diff\",\n  \"backend\": \"MD5E\",\n  \"bytesize\": \"4\",\n  \"gitshasum\": \"368ea635b9f8f468ed5a78b7dc3aa9ef846f02d3\",\n  \"has_content\": true,\n  \"humansize\": \"4 B\",\n  \"key\": \"MD5E-s4--d2d362cdc6579390f1c0617d74a7913d.txt\",\n  \"keyname\": \"d2d362cdc6579390f1c0617d74a7913d.txt\",\n  \"mtime\": \"unknown\",\n  \"objloc\": \"/tmp/differ/.git/annex/objects/Z2/91/MD5E-s4--d2d362cdc6579390f1c0617d74a7913d.txt/MD5E-s4--d2d362cdc6579390f1c0617d74a7913d.txt\",\n  \"parentds\": \"/tmp/differ\",\n  \"path\": \"/tmp/differ/demo.txt\",\n  \"prev_backend\": \"MD5E\",\n  \"prev_bytesize\": \"4\",\n  \"prev_gitshasum\": \"fb1c6ae80773fc672ac81ea7a7988415eb69daa9\",\n  \"prev_hashdirlower\": \"98d/6ca/\",\n  \"prev_hashdirmixed\": \"MX/gx/\",\n  \"prev_humansize\": \"4 B\",\n  \"prev_key\": \"MD5E-s4--ba1f2511fc30423bdbb183fe33f3dd0f.txt\",\n  \"prev_keyname\": \"ba1f2511fc30423bdbb183fe33f3dd0f.txt\",\n  \"prev_mtime\": \"unknown\",\n  \"refds\": \"/tmp/differ\",\n  \"state\": \"modified\",\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"type\": \"file\"\n}\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1562664304,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwOTU2NTYzNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2160#issuecomment-509565635"},"message":"Looked into multidiff (@yarikoptic mentioned above). Neat.\n\n```python\n\u003e\u003e\u003e from multidiff import MultidiffModel, Render\n\u003e\u003e\u003e m = MultidiffModel(['old stuff', 'old stuff with additions'])\n\u003e\u003e\u003e m.diff_last_pair()\n\u003e\u003e\u003e Render('utf8', color='html').render(m, m.diffs[0])\n\"old stuff\u003cspan class='insert'\u003e with additions\u003c/span\u003e\"\n```\n\nSadly not on PyPi, but there is a multidiff on PyPi that does something completely different.","files":null}]}